---
import Article from "../../layouts/Article.astro";
import { CHEATS, CHEATS_HOW } from "../../data/gta6-cheats";
const host = (u: string) => new URL(u).hostname.replace(/^www\./, "");
const label = { rockstar: "Rockstar", reported: "Reported", tested: "Tested by us" };
const faq = [
  { q: "Are there cheat codes in GTA 6?", a: "Not confirmed yet. Every mainline GTA game has had single-player cheat codes, but Rockstar hasn't said anything about GTA 6 cheats. We'll publish the verified list after launch." },
  { q: "Will GTA 6 cheats disable trophies or achievements?", a: "In GTA 5, using cheats disabled trophies, achievements and saving for that session. If GTA 6 follows the same pattern, expect the same restriction." },
  { q: "Can you use cheats in GTA 6 online?", a: "Cheat codes have only ever worked in single player. Using third-party cheats online breaks Rockstar's terms and can get your account banned." },
];
---
<Article
  title="GTA 6 Cheat Codes: PS5 & Xbox (Updated at Launch)"
  h1="GTA 6 Cheat Codes"
  description="Every confirmed GTA 6 cheat code for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S, added as soon as they're verified. What we know so far and how cheats worked in GTA 5."
  published="2026-10-14"
  crumbs={[{ href: "/gta-6/", label: "GTA 6" }]}
  faq={faq}
>
  {CHEATS.length === 0 ? (
    <div class="callout"><p><strong>No GTA 6 cheat codes are confirmed yet.</strong> The game launches November 19, 2026. We check for new codes every hour and add them as soon as they're verified. We won't post rumored or fake codes.</p></div>
  ) : (
    <>
      <h2>All verified GTA 6 cheat codes</h2>
      {CHEATS_HOW && <p>{CHEATS_HOW}</p>}
      <div class="table-scroll"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Effect</th><th>PS5</th><th>Xbox</th>{CHEATS.some((c) => c.phone) && <th>Phone</th>}<th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{CHEATS.map((c) => (
          <tr><td><strong>{c.effect}</strong>{c.notes && <><br /><small>{c.notes}</small></>}</td><td>{c.ps5 ?? "-"}</td><td>{c.xbox ?? "-"}</td>{CHEATS.some((x) => x.phone) && <td>{c.phone ?? "-"}</td>}<td>{label[c.verified]}<br /><small>{c.sources.map((u, i) => <>{i > 0 && " · "}<a href={u} rel="noopener">{host(u)}</a></>)}</small></td></tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Will GTA 6 have cheats?</h2>
  <p>Probably. Every mainline Grand Theft Auto game has shipped with single-player cheats, from GTA III's button codes to GTA 5's phone numbers. Rockstar hasn't confirmed anything for GTA 6 yet.</p>

  <h2>How cheats worked in GTA 5</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Button combos</strong> entered during gameplay on console.</li>
    <li><strong>Phone numbers</strong> dialed on the in-game phone, which made cheats easier to remember.</li>
    <li><strong>Trophies and achievements were disabled</strong> for the session after using a cheat, and you couldn't save while cheats were active.</li>
    <li><strong>Single player only.</strong> Cheats never worked in GTA Online.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to expect at launch</h2>
  <p>Cheat codes are usually found within hours of a GTA release. Bookmark this page. We'll add each code with the platform it works on and what it does, tested by us.</p>
  <p>Want to make money legitimately instead? The <a href="/cayo-perico-calculator/">Cayo Perico calculator</a> and <a href="/heist-cut-calculator/">heist cut calculator</a> work today.</p>
</Article>
